# Target C: fan ports enter canonical harmonic attachment cells

**Date:** 2026-10-02  
**Base main:** `1c5c0fb8aefeed7aec9e0fc6c0edd3ebf59f8326`  
**Status:** proof-only reduction. Level I and C-II remain open.

## 1. Setup

Assume the current low-outer-walk, square-root matching branch
\[
\nu(H)\le K_\nu\sqrt D,\qquad x_B\le K_x\sqrt D.
\]
The current fan theorem gives
\[
I\ge \lceil D\rceil-(4K_\nu+2K_x)\sqrt D
\tag{1}
\]
internal exact same-carrier fan vertices. Let \(T\) be the contact-degree-three
population and \(U=I-T\).

The current exact fan-flip/blocker theorem already proves that if \(U\ge I/2\),
there are at least \(I/2\) distinct strict loaded-to-diameter-inactive pairs in
\((1,1+1/D]\), including a vertex-disjoint matching of size at least \(I/22\);
it also gives at least \(I/12\) distinct inactive blocker endpoints.

This note treats the complementary case \(T\ge I/2\).

Fix a degree-three fan leaf \(p\), its carrier \(a\), adjacent leaves
\(p_-,p_+\), and third positive-contact neighbor \(z\). Put
\[
u={p-a\over D},\quad \varepsilon={1\over2D},\quad
\tau=\sqrt{1-\varepsilon^2},\quad
c_D={\varepsilon+\sqrt3\,\tau\over2}.
\tag{2}
\]

## 2. Each port is a canonical attachment incidence

The current third-neighbor theorem gives \(\deg_H(z)=0\). Hence \(z\) is
unloaded. Since \(pz\) is a positive unit contact, \(z\) lies in a canonical
unloaded positive-contact component \(I_r\), and the loaded fan leaf \(p\) is
in its attachment set \(A_r\).

The leaf \(p\) has exactly three positive contacts: the two loaded-loaded fan
contacts and \(pz\). Thus \(pz\) is its unique contact into the unloaded
subgraph. Distinct degree-three fan leaves therefore give distinct edges of the
contracted loaded/component attachment-incidence graph, even if several leaves
enter the same component.

So the degree-three side has \(T\) distinct canonical fan attachment
incidences. This removes the factor-five loss that occurs when one counts only
distinct third-neighbor vertices.

## 3. Harmonic trapping forces a deep loaded return

Canonical C-ATTACH-CURRENCY gives
\[
I_r\subseteq P_r:=\operatorname{conv}(A_r).
\tag{3}
\]
Thus \(z\in\operatorname{conv}(A_r)\). Apply the linear functional
\(x\mapsto u\cdot x\). Some \(b\in A_r\) satisfies
\[
u\cdot b\le u\cdot z.
\]
The exact inward-spoke theorem gives
\[
u\cdot(p-z)\ge c_D.
\]
Therefore
\[
\boxed{u\cdot(p-b)\ge c_D.}
\tag{4}
\]

For the adjacent fan leaves,
\[
u\cdot(p-p_-)=u\cdot(p-p_+)=\varepsilon<c_D,
\]
and \(u\cdot(p-p)=0\). Hence
\[
\boxed{b\notin\{p,p_-,p_+\}.}
\tag{5}
\]

Every port therefore forces its harmonic component to return to a nonlocal
loaded attachment at constant radial support depth.

## 4. A return on the carrier circle forces a square-root cell

Every source point lies in the closed radius-\(D\) disk centered at \(a\), so
\[
|b-a|\le D.
\tag{6}
\]

If \(b=a\), then \(p,a\in A_r\), hence
\[
\operatorname{diam}(P_r)=D.
\tag{7}
\]

Suppose \(b\ne a\) and \(|b-a|=D\). Since \(p-a=Du\),
\[
|p-b|^2
=2D\,u\cdot(p-b)
\ge2Dc_D.
\tag{8}
\]
Thus
\[
\boxed{\operatorname{diam}(P_r)\ge L_D:=\sqrt{2Dc_D}.}
\tag{9}
\]
Since \(c_D\to\sqrt3/2\),
\[
L_D=(3^{1/4}+o(1))\sqrt D.
\tag{10}
\]

If this return is another leaf \(p_{i+k}\) on the same exact fan run as
\(p=p_i\), with \(\alpha_D=\arcsin(1/(2D))\), then
\[
D(1-\cos(2k\alpha_D))\ge c_D,
\]
so
\[
k\ge{\arccos(1-c_D/D)\over2\alpha_D}
=(3^{1/4}+o(1))\sqrt D.
\tag{11}
\]
Thus a same-run return skips a square-root number of exact fan steps.

## 5. There are only O(sqrt(D)) square-root cells

Let \(\delta_r\) be the graph diameter of \(I_r\). Canonical Section 62 gives
\[
\operatorname{diam}(P_r)\le\delta_r+2
\tag{12}
\]
and
\[
\sum_r\delta_r\le6+e_{BB}+2s_C-3k,\qquad k=d_H+s_Z.
\tag{13}
\]
Because the present branch has \(c_I>0\), the pinned ledger and attachment
incidence bound give
\[
c_I+e_{BB}+s_C=q-2+k,\qquad s_C\le q-c_I-2.
\tag{14}
\]
Substitution yields
\[
\sum_r\delta_r
\le2q+2-2c_I-2k
\le2q
\le2\pi D.
\tag{15}
\]

Hence the number \(N_L\) of components with
\(\operatorname{diam}(P_r)\ge L_D\) obeys
\[
\boxed{N_L\le {2\pi D\over L_D-2}
=\left({2\pi\over3^{1/4}}+o(1)\right)\sqrt D.}
\tag{16}
\]

## 6. Global harmonic-return fork

Assume \(T\ge I/2\). For every degree-three leaf choose a return \(b(p)\)
satisfying (4).

Call the incidence **off-carrier** if
\[
b(p)\ne a(p),\qquad |b(p)-a(p)|<D.
\tag{17}
\]
Otherwise Section 4 places it in a cell of diameter at least \(L_D\).

If at least \(T/2\) incidences are off-carrier, then there are at least
\[
\boxed{I/4}
\tag{18}
\]
distinct canonical fan attachment incidences with an off-carrier loaded return
satisfying (4). The return vertices themselves need not be distinct.

Otherwise at least \(T/2\ge I/4\) incidences lie in \(L_D\)-large cells.
By (16), one component \(I_*\) contains at least
\[
\boxed{
{I(L_D-2)\over8\pi D}
=
\left({3^{1/4}\over8\pi}-o(1)\right)\sqrt D
}
\tag{19}
\]
distinct degree-three fan leaves among its loaded attachment vertices, and
\[
\operatorname{diam}(P_*)\ge
(3^{1/4}+o(1))\sqrt D.
\tag{20}
\]

Combining with the fan-flip theorem, the current low-\(x_B\),
square-root-matching branch now has only three alternatives:

1. a linear vertex-disjoint inverse-\(D\) almost-unit matching from loaded fan
   leaves to diameter-inactive interior blockers;
2. a linear family of canonical fan attachment incidences with off-carrier
   deep loaded returns; or
3. one square-root-diameter harmonic cell carrying a square-root population of
   exact diameter-fan attachment vertices.

## 7. Remaining bottleneck

This does not close C-II.

In alternative 2, the return vertices may be reused, so the next missing theorem
must convert the linear support-depth incidences into a planar-incidence,
perimeter, or diameter-thrackle obstruction.

In alternative 3, the forced cell is only square-root scale. The next target is
to combine its square-root fan attachment population with noncrossing attachment
order and the actual diameter thrackle, with the aim of forcing a diameter-scale
cell, linear outer-walk defect, an exact unit triangle, or a same-cardinality
strict sub-\(D\) replacement.

**Disposition:** exact proof-only coupling to canonical C-ATTACH-CURRENCY. No
numerical experiment, verifier execution, CI result, or unexecuted certificate
is used.
